# textures_backing_ref: An IOSurface backing in task 0 (type 4: one BGRA plane of 4x4 at +0x100 of its pages) and three textures over it in task 1 (type 5, commandTypes 12, 47 and 57). Each pages in through the backing (a ref texture forwards prepare, synchronize and validity to it): a copy out shows the guest bytes; a fill with flags 6 lands in task 0's pages; opcode 53 on task 0 names the backing itself; invalidateHost re-reads. Opcode 54 deletes the backing from task 0's list (a taskID other than 0 faults, "This command may only reference a kernel task"); the textures keep theirs. 63 on a ref texture does nothing (it does not support discard); 63 on task 0 discards the backing's transfer buffer; with neither copy marked valid by 52, the next prepare logs "Trying to prepare backing from invalid guest" and pages the guest bytes in. In-process only: in the service the backing lookup aborts (textures_backing_ref_service).
